<article id="credits" class="about-closing-block">
<p class="eyebrow">Credits</p>
<h2>Credits and acknowledgements</h2>
<p>Galapagensis is an independent research programme, but its work depends upon the institutions, repositories, communities, researchers, families, and individuals who preserve documentary traces, make collections accessible, share knowledge, answer questions, identify people and places, and contribute evidence to ongoing research.</p>
<p>Specific sources, collections, contributions, collaborations, and permissions are credited where they are used.</p>
</article>

<article id="contact" class="about-closing-block">
<p class="eyebrow">Contact</p>
<h2>Contact Galapagensis</h2>
<p>Galapagensis welcomes contact from researchers, archives, libraries, museums, scientific collections, communities, families, private collectors, and others who hold or know of material related to the history of the Galápagos Islands.</p>
<p>Contact is also welcome from individuals and institutions interested in research collaboration, documentary exchange, access to collections, or contributing knowledge to an existing investigation.</p>
<a class="text-link" href="#">Contact Galapagensis</a>
</article>

